error[NK1214]: `t` is cut with brackets, `t[0..]`, and a text takes no `[…]`: it is cut by name, at its own positions (ADR-374 D3).
  --> tests/text_bracket_cut_is_refused.nika:6:5
   |
 6 |     println(t[0..<t.len()])
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = note: Brackets count elements, and a boundary in a text is not one; `Bytes` and lists keep `[a..<b]` with numbers.
   = help: Cut at a match with `t.before(m.start)`, `t.after(m.end)` or `t.between(p, q)`; or say the view: `t.bytes[0..].text()` for bytes, `t.graphemes.take(t.len())` for what a reader sees.
